WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
A lighthouse holds

c2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:02.325
just one lamp,

c3
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:03.250
yet ships far

c4
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:03.875
out at sea

c5
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:04.675
can see it.

c6
00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:05.125
How?

c7
00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:06.100
On its own,

c8
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.125
a flame spills

c9
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:07.925
light in every

c10
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:08.725
direction,

c11
00:00:08.725 --> 00:00:09.400
and most of

c12
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.300
it never reaches

c13
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:10.875
a ship.

c14
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:12.325
So Augustin Fresnel

c15
00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:13.100
wrapped the lamp

c16
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:13.700
in rings of

c17
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.425
glass.

c18
00:00:14.425 --> 00:00:15.375
The central rings

c19
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:16.050
bend the light

c20
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.050
into one straight

c21
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:17.600
beam.

c22
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.600
The outer prisms

c23
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.450
catch the steep

c24
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.150
rays,

c25
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.175
reflect them inside

c26
00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:22.050
the glass,

c27
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:22.700
and add them

c28
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:23.225
to the same

c29
00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:23.750
beam.

c30
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.450
Then the whole

c31
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.975
lens slowly turns,

c32
00:00:25.975 --> 00:00:26.725
and far out

c33
00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:27.525
at sea,

c34
00:00:27.525 --> 00:00:28.325
sailors see the

c35
00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:29.350
beam sweep past

c36
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:29.925
as a bright

c37
00:00:29.925 --> 00:00:30.300
flash.

